title: 'hrmp: return deposits and request counts when offboarding drops open channel requests'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    Open channel requests removed at a session change because a para offboards no longer leak
    deposits or request counts:

    - A confirmed request that can't be turned into a channel, because one of its paras is
      already offboarding, gives both deposits back instead of keeping them reserved.
    - When a request is cleaned up because one of its paras is outgoing, the sender's deposit and,
      for a confirmed request, the recipient's deposit are given back, including to the outgoing
      para itself, as already happens for the deposits of its channels.
    - The sender's open request count is decremented when only the recipient offboards, so the
      request no longer takes one of the sender's outbound channel slots.
    - No recipient deposit is given back for channels with or amongst the system, since none is
      taken for them.

    The weight of the request cleanup is benchmarked with confirmed requests, which is now the
    worst case.

    No storage, API or configuration change. Deposits already left reserved and request counts
    already leaked by earlier versions are not touched.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
